We are pleased to announce the implementation of **Secret Protection** capabilities as part of our security measures. This new feature uses GitHub Advanced Security functionalities to prevent the accidental exposure of sensitive information such as API keys, passwords, tokens, and other secrets in your repositories.

### What's Changing?

We have implemented Push Protection and Secret Scanning mechanisms to help reduce the exposure of sensitive information in our repositories.

When code containing a potential secret is pushed, a notification will appear and the push will be blocked. The developer may request a bypass if necessary. Additionally, Secret Scanning sends email alerts when such exposures are detected, and CISOs can review all cases in the Security section.

### Why Is This Important?

This change minimizes the risk of secrets being exposed in the repositories.

### How to Use This Feature?

Components in Gluon GitHub Organizations will automatically be enabled with this improvement. 